sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Client as Client
    participant Router as chi Router
    participant G as middlewares.RequirePermission
    participant S as ScopeBinding
    participant Per as perms.PermissionService
    participant Repo as permstorage.PostgresRepository
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant H as Next Handler

    Note over Router,G: Registration time - runs once while routes are built
    Router->>G: RequireGlobal / RequireOrganization / RequireProject
    G->>G: build ScopeBinding with scope + entity + IDExtractor
    G-->>Router: handler returned - no validation here any more

    Note over Client,H: Request time - per request
    Client->>Router: HTTP Request
    Note over Router: Authenticate runs first and puts userID in context
    Router->>G: guard(next)(w, r)
    activate G

    Note over G: Step 1 - Binding validation - now inside the handler
    G->>S: binding.Validate(permission) and binding.allows(permission)
    alt entity scope without Extract
        S-->>G: Validate error
        G-->>Client: 500 Internal - authentication required
    else permission is global but scope is not global
        S-->>G: allows returns false
        G-->>Client: 500 Internal - authentication required
    else binding is valid
        S-->>G: nil and true
        Note over G: Step 2 - Identity
        G->>G: GetCurrentUserID(r.Context())
        alt no userID in context
            G-->>Client: 401 Unauthorized - authentication required
        else identity resolved
            Note over G: Step 3 - Scope
            G->>G: ScopeContext type = binding.Scope resourceType = binding.Entity
            alt EntityScoped(scope)
                G->>G: binding.Extract(r) via URLParam or QueryParam or ParamOrQuery or ChainIDExtractors
                alt id cannot be resolved
                    G-->>Client: 400 Invalid - cannot resolve scope for this request
                else id resolved
                    G->>G: set ScopeID - never widen the scope
                end
            else global scope
                G->>G: scope ids stay empty - the query matches only the global branch
            end

            Note over G: Step 4 - one IsAllowed call for every scope
            G->>Per: IsAllowed(ctx, userID, permission, scope)
            activate Per
            Per->>Per: if permission.IsGlobal then scope becomes global only
            Per->>Repo: GetPermissionsForUser(ctx, userID, scope)
            activate Repo
            Repo->>DB: single query - CTE target and resolved<br/>org falls back to the project owner<br/>global or organization or project in one pass
            DB-->>Repo: rows of role_scope and permission ref
            Note over Repo: drop global permissions granted at non global scope<br/>dedupe by ID and Name
            Repo-->>Per: []Permission
            deactivate Repo
            Per->>Per: HasPermissionGranted - direct match then Implies transitively
            alt permission granted
                Per-->>G: true, nil
            else not granted
                Per-->>G: false, nil
            end
            deactivate Per

            Note over G: Step 5 - Decision
            alt isAllowed and err is nil
                G->>H: next.ServeHTTP(w, r)
                activate H
                H-->>Client: 2xx
                deactivate H
            else err is not nil
                G-->>Client: 403 Forbidden - permissions unexpected error
            else isAllowed is false
                G-->>Client: 403 Forbidden - permissions denied
            end
        end
    end
    deactivate G

    Note over G: authorize.go L45-49 Validate inside the handler 500 - L50-53 scope mismatch 500<br/>L54-58 identity 401 - L60-73 scope build 400<br/>L75 the single IsAllowed call shared by every scope - L77-80 lookup error 403 - L81-84 denial 403 - L86 next handler<br/>validation moved out of registration so a misconfigured guard no longer panics at startup<br/>it now costs every request a recheck and returns 500 instead of failing the build<br/>every guard branch writes through response.Error then returns - the helper is omitted here

    Note over Repo: get_permissions_for_user.go L10-48 one statement for all three scopes<br/>L11-24 target and resolved CTEs - org falls back to the project owner<br/>L62-69 scope ids are passed empty rather than NULL so the CTE guards on empty<br/>L94-96 global permission dropped unless roleScope is global - L98-106 dedupe by ID and Name<br/>no index exists yet on assigned_roles or group_members
